WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.619
Hi. Let me show you how to check whether your agent's promises match what its tools actually did.

2
00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:18.253
I start a new eval and open Write with AI. I describe the mistake in plain English: telling a guest their room is booked, when the reservation tool never confirmed it.

3
00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:24.114
It writes a complete judge prompt for me. I read it through, and accept it.

4
00:00:25.064 --> 00:00:32.692
One change matters here. Instead of three separate fields, I let it read the whole conversation, tool results included.

5
00:00:33.642 --> 00:00:37.926
I keep it pass or fail, and save it as booking claim check.

6
00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:46.687
Now I test it on real traffic. I pick my booking project, choose sessions, and map the conversation to the session's traces.

7
00:00:53.836 --> 00:00:56.031
Then I run it on Maya's booking.

8
00:00:56.996 --> 00:01:02.795
Maya passes. The tool confirmed her booking, and the agent gave her the same confirmation number.

9
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:13.189
Now, the same check on Daniel.

10
00:01:16.196 --> 00:01:27.194
Daniel fails. The agent told him his room was reserved, but the tool had only placed a hold while his payment was pending. That's the kind of promise you want to catch before a guest does.
